Variables are numeric,  string,  character,  or  boolean  values.
Boolean  variables  are set merely by specifying their name; they
may be reset by prepending a ‘!’ to  the  name.   Other  variable
types  are set by concatenating an ‘=’ and the value.  The entire
assignment must not have any blanks in it.  A single set  command
may  be used to interrogate as well as set a number of variables.
Variables may be initialized at run time by placing set  commands
(without  the  ‘‘˜s’’  prefix in a file in one’s home directory).
